- **`Verse(n)`** returns one verse ending in `"\n"`. Verses 2, 1 and 0 are special cases. Any `n` outside 0–99 returns an error.
- **`Verses(start, stop)`** counts down from `start` to `stop`. It adds a blank line after each verse. It returns an error if either bound is out of range or if `start < stop`.
